{{!
    @template local_awareness/manage/cell_title

    The Title cell: the notice title, with the pages it applies to underneath.

    A notice title has no length cap in the database, so the cell clamps it to two lines in CSS and
    carries the whole string in the title attribute. The full text stays in the node — clipped for
    the eye, intact for a screen reader.

    The title arrives already through format_string(), which resolves the text filters and applies
    core's HTML cleaning, so it is emitted with a triple stash: escaping it again would show a
    multilang or emphasised title as literal markup. The path is the opposite case — a URL pattern
    rather than prose — so it arrives RAW and is escaped here by Mustache.

    Context variables required:
    * title (string) — the filtered notice title, safe HTML
    * titleplain (string) — the same title for the tooltip attribute
    * where (string) — the raw path pattern, or the "anywhere" sentence

    Example context (json):
    {
        "title": "Scheduled maintenance",
        "titleplain": "Scheduled maintenance",
        "where": "/course/view.php%"
    }
}}
<span class="local-awareness-celltitle" title="{{titleplain}}">{{{title}}}</span>
<span class="local-awareness-subline" title="{{where}}">{{where}}</span>
